---@field pausingConsented? boolean Whether pausing is allowed for the proposal. This is a negotiable term between buyers and publishers.
---@field isRenegotiating? boolean Output only. True if the proposal was previously finalized and is now being renegotiated.
---@field billedBuyer? string Output only. When the client field is populated, this field refers to the buyer who creates and manages the client buyer and gets billed on behalf of the client buyer; when the buyer field is populated, this field is the same value as buyer. Format : `buyers/{buyerAccountId}`
---@field sellerContacts? gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.ContactList Output only. Contact information for the seller.
---@field buyerPrivateData? gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.PrivateData Buyer private data (hidden from seller).
---@field originatorRole? gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.ProposalOriginatorRoleEnum|string Output only. Indicates whether the buyer/seller created the proposal.
---@field buyerContacts? gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.ContactList Contact information for the buyer.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time when the proposal was last revised.
---@field dealType? gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.ProposalDealTypeEnum|string Output only. Type of deal the proposal contains.
---@field notes? gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.NoteList A list of notes from the buyer and the seller attached to this proposal.
---@field proposalRevision? string Output only. The revision number for the proposal. Each update to the proposal or deal causes the proposal revision number to auto-increment. The buyer keeps track of the last revision number they know of and pass it in when making an update. If the head revision number on the server has since incremented, then an ABORTED error is returned during the update operation to let the buyer know that a subsequent update was made.
---@field termsAndConditions? string Output only. The terms and conditions associated with this proposal. Accepting a proposal implies acceptance of this field. This is created by the seller, the buyer can only view it.
---@field buyer? string Output only. Refers to a buyer in The Realtime-bidding API. Format: `buyers/{buyerAccountId}`
---@field publisherProfile? string Immutable. Reference to the seller on the proposal. Format: `buyers/{buyerAccountId}/publisherProfiles/{publisherProfileId}` Note: This field may be set only when creating the resource. Modifying this field while updating the resource will result in an error.
---@field displayName? string Output only. The descriptive name for the proposal. Maximum length of 255 unicode characters is allowed. Control characters are not allowed. Buyers cannot update this field. Note: Not to be confused with name, which is a unique identifier of the proposal.
---@field client? string Output only. Refers to a Client. Format: `buyers/{buyerAccountId}/clients/{clientAccountid}`
---@field state? gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.ProposalStateEnum|string Output only. Indicates the state of the proposal.
---@field name string Immutable. The name of the proposal serving as a unique identifier. Format: buyers/{accountId}/proposals/{proposalId}
---@field updateMask? string List of fields to be updated. If empty or unspecified, the service will update all fields populated in the update request excluding the output only fields and primitive fields with default value. Note that explicit field mask is required in order to reset a primitive field back to its default value, for example, false for boolean fields, 0 for integer fields. A special field mask consisting of a single path "*" can be used to indicate full replacement(the equivalent of PUT method), updatable fields unset or unspecified in the input will be cleared or set to default value. Output only fields will be ignored regardless of the value of updateMask.

