---Pricing terms for Programmatic Guaranteed Deals.
---@class gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.ProgrammaticGuaranteedTerms
---@field fixedPrice? gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.Price Fixed price for the deal.
---@field minimumDailyLooks? string Daily minimum looks for CPD deal types. For CPD deals, buyer should negotiate on this field instead of guaranteed_looks.
---@field guaranteedLooks? string Count of guaranteed looks. For CPD deals, buyer changes to guaranteed_looks will be ignored.
---@field percentShareOfVoice? string For sponsorship deals, this is the percentage of the seller's eligible impressions that the deal will serve until the cap is reached. Valid value is within range 0~100.
---@field impressionCap? string The lifetime impression cap for CPM Sponsorship deals. Deal will stop serving when cap is reached.
---@field reservationType? gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.ProgrammaticGuaranteedTermsReservationTypeEnum|string The reservation type for a Programmatic Guaranteed deal. This indicates whether the number of impressions is fixed, or a percent of available impressions. If not specified, the default reservation type is STANDARD.

---@alias gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.ProgrammaticGuaranteedTermsReservationTypeEnum "RESERVATION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"STANDARD"|"SPONSORSHIP"

---Represents a proposal in the Marketplace. A proposal is the unit of negotiation between a seller and a buyer.
---@class gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.Proposal
---@field lastUpdaterOrCommentorRole? gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.ProposalLastUpdaterOrCommentorRoleEnum Output only. The role of the last user that either updated the proposal or left a comment.
---@field pausingConsented? boolean Whether pausing is allowed for the proposal. This is a negotiable term between buyers and publishers.
---@field isRenegotiating? boolean Output only. True if the proposal was previously finalized and is now being renegotiated.
---@field billedBuyer? string Output only. When the client field is populated, this field refers to the buyer who creates and manages the client buyer and gets billed on behalf of the client buyer; when the buyer field is populated, this field is the same value as buyer. Format : `buyers/{buyerAccountId}`
---@field sellerContacts? gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.ContactList Output only. Contact information for the seller.
---@field buyerPrivateData? gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.PrivateData Buyer private data (hidden from seller).
---@field originatorRole? gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.ProposalOriginatorRoleEnum Output only. Indicates whether the buyer/seller created the proposal.
---@field buyerContacts? gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.ContactList Contact information for the buyer.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time when the proposal was last revised.
---@field name? string Immutable. The name of the proposal serving as a unique identifier. Format: buyers/{accountId}/proposals/{proposalId}
---@field dealType? gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.ProposalDealTypeEnum Output only. Type of deal the proposal contains.
---@field notes? gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.NoteList A list of notes from the buyer and the seller attached to this proposal.
---@field proposalRevision? string Output only. The revision number for the proposal. Each update to the proposal or deal causes the proposal revision number to auto-increment. The buyer keeps track of the last revision number they know of and pass it in when making an update. If the head revision number on the server has since incremented, then an ABORTED error is returned during the update operation to let the buyer know that a subsequent update was made.
---@field termsAndConditions? string Output only. The terms and conditions associated with this proposal. Accepting a proposal implies acceptance of this field. This is created by the seller, the buyer can only view it.
---@field buyer? string Output only. Refers to a buyer in The Realtime-bidding API. Format: `buyers/{buyerAccountId}`
---@field publisherProfile? string Immutable. Reference to the seller on the proposal. Format: `buyers/{buyerAccountId}/publisherProfiles/{publisherProfileId}` Note: This field may be set only when creating the resource. Modifying this field while updating the resource will result in an error.
---@field displayName? string Output only. The descriptive name for the proposal. Maximum length of 255 unicode characters is allowed. Control characters are not allowed. Buyers cannot update this field. Note: Not to be confused with name, which is a unique identifier of the proposal.
---@field client? string Output only. Refers to a Client. Format: `buyers/{buyerAccountId}/clients/{clientAccountid}`
---@field state? gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.ProposalStateEnum Output only. Indicates the state of the proposal.

---@alias gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.ProposalDealTypeEnum "DEAL_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PREFERRED_DEAL"|"PRIVATE_AUCTION"|"PROGRAMMATIC_GUARANTEED"

---@alias gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.ProposalLastUpdaterOrCommentorRoleEnum "BUYER_SELLER_ROLE_UNSPECIFIED"|"BUYER"|"SELLER"

---@alias gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.ProposalList gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.Proposal[]

---@alias gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.ProposalOriginatorRoleEnum "BUYER_SELLER_ROLE_UNSPECIFIED"|"BUYER"|"SELLER"

---@alias gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.ProposalStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"BUYER_REVIEW_REQUESTED"|"SELLER_REVIEW_REQUESTED"|"BUYER_ACCEPTANCE_REQUESTED"|"FINALIZED"|"TERMINATED"

---The values in the publisher profile are supplied by the publisher. All fields are not filterable unless stated otherwise.
---@class gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.PublisherProfile
---@field name? string Name of the publisher profile. Format: `buyers/{buyer}/publisherProfiles/{publisher_profile}`
---@field mediaKitUrl? string URL to additional marketing and sales materials.
---@field overview? string Overview of the publisher.
---@field displayName? string Display name of the publisher profile. Can be used to filter the response of the publisherProfiles.list method.
---@field topHeadlines? gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.StringList Up to three key metrics and rankings. For example, "#1 Mobile News Site for 20 Straight Months".
---@field programmaticDealsContact? string Contact information for programmatic deals. This is free text entered by the publisher and may include information like names, phone numbers and email addresses.
---@field isParent? boolean Indicates if this profile is the parent profile of the seller. A parent profile represents all the inventory from the seller, as opposed to child profile that is created to brand a portion of inventory. One seller has only one parent publisher profile, and can have multiple child profiles. See https://support.google.com/admanager/answer/6035806 for details. Can be used to filter the response of the publisherProfiles.list method by setting the filter to "is_parent: true".
---@field mobileApps? gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.PublisherProfileMobileApplicationList The list of apps represented in this publisher profile. Empty if this is a parent profile.
---@field logoUrl? string A Google public URL to the logo for this publisher profile. The logo is stored as a PNG, JPG, or GIF image.
---@field audienceDescription? string Description on the publisher's audience.
---@field domains? gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.StringList The list of domains represented in this publisher profile. Empty if this is a parent profile. These are top private domains, meaning that these will not contain a string like "photos.google.co.uk/123", but will instead contain "google.co.uk". Can be used to filter the response of the publisherProfiles.list method.
---@field directDealsContact? string Contact information for direct reservation deals. This is free text entered by the publisher and may include information like names, phone numbers and email addresses.
---@field publisherCode? string A unique identifying code for the seller. This value is the same for all of the seller's parent and child publisher profiles. Can be used to filter the response of the publisherProfiles.list method.
---@field pitchStatement? string Statement explaining what's unique about publisher's business, and why buyers should partner with the publisher.
---@field samplePageUrl? string URL to a sample content page.

---@alias gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.PublisherProfileList gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.PublisherProfile[]

---A mobile application that contains a external app ID, name, and app store.
---@class gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.PublisherProfileMobileApplication
---@field appStore? gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.PublisherProfileMobileApplicationAppStoreEnum The app store the app belongs to. Can be used to filter the response of the publisherProfiles.list method.
---@field name? string The name of the app.
---@field externalAppId? string The external ID for the app from its app store. Can be used to filter the response of the publisherProfiles.list method.

---@alias gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.PublisherProfileMobileApplicationAppStoreEnum "APP_STORE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"APPLE_ITUNES"|"GOOGLE_PLAY"|"ROKU"|"AMAZON_FIRE_TV"|"PLAYSTATION"|"XBOX"|"SAMSUNG_TV"|"AMAZON"|"OPPO"|"SAMSUNG"|"VIVO"|"XIAOMI"|"LG_TV"

---@alias gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.PublisherProfileMobileApplicationList gcp.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1.PublisherProfileMobileApplication[]

